{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"alias":"uncovered-vincible-turkey","creation_channel":"cli","description":"`_compose_files()` in `tasks.py:13-17` builds a fixed `-f compose.yaml [-f compose.override.yaml]` argument list. Passing explicit `-f` flags overrides the `COMPOSE_FILE` environment variable, so every `inv` task that shells out to Compose operates on a different projection of the stack than the one the operator started.\n\nThe running stack on the pilot machine carries a third overlay. `docker inspect` reports `com.docker.compose.project.config_files` as `compose.yaml,compose.override.yaml,compose.massgov.yaml`. `inv up`, `inv down`, `inv stop`, `inv logs`, `inv migrate`, `inv db-reset`, and `_run_scripted` all drop that third file.\n\nRecreating services without the overlay moves published ports back to their base values, drops the target repository mounts the workers need, and re-enables services the overlay disables by profile. On this machine the overlay places `schedule-bootstrap` in a disabled profile, so an `inv up` would install the Temporal intake schedule and begin unattended intake.\n\nDocker Compose already resolves `COMPOSE_FILE` from the project `.env`, verified with a probe. The extension point exists and the task runner bypasses it. Honouring it keeps the mechanism generic, because the platform learns nothing about any particular overlay.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The compose argument list is empty when `COMPOSE_FILE` is set, so Compose resolves the file list itself, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_tasks_compose.py -k compose_files_defers_to_the_compose_file_environment_variable`\n- [ ] The compose argument list falls back to the base file when `COMPOSE_FILE` is unset, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_tasks_compose.py -k compose_files_falls_back_to_the_base_file`\n- [ ] The compose argument list adds the override file when it exists and `COMPOSE_FILE` is unset, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_tasks_compose.py -k compose_files_adds_the_override_file_when_present`\n- [ ] A `COMPOSE_FILE` value defined only in the project `.env` is honoured, proven by `pytest tests/unit/test_tasks_compose.py -k compose_files_reads_the_compose_file_variable_from_the_env_file`\n\n## Testing\nRun each acceptance criterion selector on its own. Run `PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/inv ci` before closing the ticket.","id":"41e9-7091-dd2c-44d0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["adp","compose","tooling"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Honour COMPOSE_FILE in the invoke task runner so inv tasks target the running stack"},"env_id":"8c3ef925-fbdc-4d88-8d59-f391cf59568c","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1790012253819771001,"uuid":"9f7f1e1b-b3cb-47dc-ad74-40d77952b461"}